Respiratory rhythm generation centre is located at pre-Botzinger complex of the medulla.
Respiratory centre: It is located in the medulla oblongata. It is composed of: - Dorsal respiratory group of neurons - Ventral respiratory group of neurons - Pre-Botzinger complex (PB) - Pneumotaxic centre (PC) - Apneustic centre - Apneustic centre is located in the pons. It is the only respiratory centre which is not located in the medulla oblongata. It is also called the pontine respiratory centre.

